# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository regardless of the
# platform a contributor works on. Windows checkouts still get CRLF in the
# working tree; only what is stored is fixed. This repo has been LF-clean
# since its first commit and currently stays that way only because Git for
# Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default -- this makes it the repo's rule
# rather than one machine's setting.
* text=auto

# Images are never text. `* text=auto` above only keeps PNGs safe because git
# happens to sniff a NUL byte in the header; two committed icons were found
# corrupt (invalid image data), so say so explicitly instead of relying on a
# heuristic -- no end-of-line conversion or diff/merge treatment, ever.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
